    <string name="dialog_faq_title">❓  FAQ</string>
    <string name="dialog_faq_msg">Q: Which APK formats are supported?\nA: Any standard APK file (.apk).\n\nQ: Which signature formats are supported?\nA: PKCS12 (.p12 / .pfx) and platform key pairs (.pk8 + .pem). JKS and BKS are not supported.\n\nQ: Why does the output APK size differ slightly?\nA: The original signature is changed and the manifest is re-encoded + patched.\n\nQ: What\'s the patching process?\nA: The AndroidManifest.xml file will be patched for removing or disabling trackers and ads.\n\nQ: The app shows \"Manifest pre-load failed\". What does it mean?\nA: The APK may be encrypted or use a non-standard binary XML format.</string>
